**The BUG — shared ArrayList inside forEach:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG: mutating shared list inside forEach
List<String> results = new ArrayList<>();  // shared mutable state!
trades.stream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .map(Trade::getSymbol)
    .forEach(results::add);  // side effect: mutating external list!

// Sequential: WORKS by accident (single thread)
// Parallel: BROKEN!
List<String> results = new ArrayList<>();
trades.parallelStream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .map(Trade::getSymbol)
    .forEach(results::add);  // 💥 ConcurrentModificationException or LOST ELEMENTS!
// ArrayList is NOT thread-safe — concurrent add() corrupts internal array
```

**The FIX — collect() (thread-safe by design):**

```java
// ✅ CORRECT: collect() handles accumulation internally
List<String> results = trades.stream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .map(Trade::getSymbol)
    .collect(Collectors.toList());  // thread-safe accumulation!

// Parallel: STILL CORRECT!
List<String> results = trades.parallelStream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .map(Trade::getSymbol)
    .collect(Collectors.toList());
// collect() uses: supplier (ArrayList::new per thread), accumulator (add), combiner (addAll)
// Each thread has its OWN local list → merged at the end → no shared mutation!
```

**Side effects in map/filter — even worse:**

```java
// ❌ TERRIBLE: side effect inside map()
List<String> auditLog = new ArrayList<>();
List<BigDecimal> amounts = trades.stream()
    .filter(t -> {
        auditLog.add("checked: " + t.getTradeId());  // side effect in filter!
        return t.isSettled();
    })
    .map(t -> {
        auditLog.add("mapped: " + t.getTradeId());   // side effect in map!
        return t.getAmount();
    })
    .toList();
// Problem 1: In parallel → auditLog is corrupted
// Problem 2: JVM might skip peek/filter calls for optimization
// Problem 3: Order of auditLog entries is unpredictable
```

**reduce() — also side-effect-free:**

```java
// ✅ CORRECT: reduce produces result without external mutation
BigDecimal total = trades.stream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .map(Trade::getAmount)
    .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);
// No shared mutable state — reduce accumulates internally
```

